WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Module review · Marketing & Communications
Recap: Marketing & Communications

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Bring objectives, audiences, messages and channels together in one plan you can run from launch.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.393
You planned how to reach the people your idea needs: a strategy linked to your objectives, priority audiences, clear messages, ethical stories, channels you can sustain, a launch campaign and measures of what helps.

4
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:28.393
One lesson at a time

5
00:00:28.393 --> 00:00:36.289
8.1 Communications strategy: A communications strategy serves your strategic objectives and stops scarce time going on noise.

6
00:00:36.289 --> 00:00:45.296
8.2 Audiences and segmentation: Communication starts with what each audience needs to understand or do, grouped from your stakeholder map.

7
00:00:45.296 --> 00:00:55.304
8.3 Messaging framework: A core message, a few supporting messages with proof and audience versions keep everyone saying the essentials.

8
00:00:55.704 --> 00:00:56.304
One lesson at a time

9
00:00:56.304 --> 00:01:06.422
8.4 Storytelling and ethical storytelling: Before stories of change exist, you can tell the problem and why you started, truthfully and with consent.

10
00:01:06.422 --> 00:01:16.170
8.5 Website, SEO and discoverability: Your website is where people check you are real, relevant and trustworthy, especially when you are new.

11
00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:25.067
8.6 Social media: One social channel done well, where your audiences already are, beats five done badly.

12
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:26.067
One lesson at a time

13
00:01:26.067 --> 00:01:36.556
8.7 Email, newsletters and supporter journeys: Email builds a relationship you own; fifty people who asked to hear from you beat a borrowed list.

14
00:01:36.556 --> 00:01:46.304
8.8 Content strategy and editorial calendar: Three to five content pillars linked to your objectives keep what you publish focused and sustainable.

15
00:01:46.304 --> 00:01:57.422
8.9 Campaigns and calls to action: A campaign is a time-bound push for one result from one audience, often starting with your launch.

16
00:01:57.822 --> 00:01:58.422
One lesson at a time

17
00:01:58.422 --> 00:02:08.170
8.10 Community building and engagement: A community connects people to your cause and to each other, widening reach and testing your ideas.

18
00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:17.919
8.11 Media relations and press materials: When nobody knows you yet, timely, local, human stories with credible evidence can earn useful coverage.

19
00:02:17.919 --> 00:02:30.148
8.12 Reputation, crisis communication and social media policy: With little reputation to fall back on, one problem can define you, so crisis essentials come before launch.

20
00:02:30.548 --> 00:02:31.148
One lesson at a time

21
00:02:31.148 --> 00:02:41.526
8.13 Measuring communications performance: Reach and likes are easy to count but rarely the goal; what matters is whether people act.

22
00:02:42.126 --> 00:02:54.726
Protect makes your plans hold up: financial management turns your activities, campaigns and team into budgets and cash flow, and legal and risk work keeps them safe.

23
00:02:55.326 --> 00:03:00.126
You check your communications plan and download each exercise as a PDF.

24
00:03:01.626 --> 00:03:04.726
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
